    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nA remarkable two-storey thatched cottage complemented by exceptional gardens and grounds\n\nSet amidst beautifully maintained gardens and grounds, Tearmann is an enchanting thatched cottage residence complemented by a detached guest cottage, a substantial workshop and studio building, and a traditional stone outbuilding, creating a highly versatile country property of exceptional appeal.\n\nSet behind decorative wrought iron gates and colourful flowering borders, the beautifully preserved thatched cottage occupies the heart of an attractive courtyard setting framed by traditional stone buildings. The sweeping thatched roof, natural stone elevations and heritage-painted doors create an immediately captivating first impression, while mature planting and established hedgerows provide privacy and lend a wonderful sense of arrival.\n\nEntered through a traditional timber door painted in a heritage green, the welcoming entrance porch immediately sets the tone for the accommodation within. Flagstone flooring, whitewashed stone walls and exposed timber ceilings combine to create a wonderful sense of authenticity, while a central hallway draws the eye through the cottage towards the main reception room beyond.\n\nThe heart of the home is a magnificent open-plan kitchen, dining and living room, a light-filled space defined by its double-height vaulted ceiling, exposed timber finishes and warm wooden flooring. Rich in atmosphere and character, the room centres around an impressive inglenook fireplace crafted from natural stone and brick, creating a striking focal point and a wonderfully inviting place in which to gather. Traditional country-style cabinetry complements the heritage of the cottage, while the generous proportions and open-plan layout provide an ideal setting for family living and entertaining. A staircase rises from the main reception space to one of the first-floor bedrooms tucked beneath the eaves.\n\nComplementing the living area is a charming sitting room/snug, a wonderfully inviting room perfectly suited to use as a reading room, library or private sitting room. Exposed timber beams, fitted bookcases and warm timber flooring lend a sense of comfort and character, while the stove-effect fireplace provides an attractive focal point. Together, these features create a peaceful retreat distinct from the openness of the main living space.\n\nThe remaining accommodation within the main residence is arranged off the central hallway and includes a spacious ground-floor bedroom and family bathroom. The first floor provides a further bedroom beneath the thatched roof, with both rooms enjoying attractive views across the gardens.\n\nA particularly appealing feature of the property is the detached guest cottage, extending to approximately 94 sq m and offering exceptional flexibility for visiting family, multigenerational living or guest accommodation. Double doors open into a bright open-plan kitchen, dining and living area with vaulted ceilings and an abundance of natural light. A separate reception room provides additional living space with direct access to the courtyard and gardens. The ground floor also incorporates a wet room and a cosy sitting room, while the first floor is arranged as a generous double bedroom overlooking the accommodation below.\n\nPositioned adjacent to the courtyard is a substantial stone-built workshop and studio. The building comprises a bright studio and a spacious workshop, both benefiting from excellent natural light and impressive ceiling heights. The versatility of the accommodation lends itself to a variety of uses including creative, recreational, craft or home-business purposes.\n\nCompleting the collection of buildings is a traditional stone outbuilding connected to the main cottage. Subject to the necessary planning consents, it offers significant potential for conversion, alternative use, or integration into the main residence.\n\nThe gardens at Tearmann are a defining feature of the property and have been lovingly nurtured over many years to create a landscape of exceptional beauty and horticultural interest. Mature specimen trees, flowering shrubs and carefully curated planting provide colour, texture and fragrance throughout the seasons, with highlights including Chilean Firetree, Magnolia stellata, Camellias, Daphne 'Perfume Princess', Hydrangeas, Corkscrew Hazel and Hawthorn. Fragrant Summer Jasmine and Clematis weave throughout the garden, while climbing and rambling roses create spectacular seasonal displays. Expansive lawns, beautifully stocked borders and sheltered seating areas combine to create a setting of remarkable tranquillity and privacy, reflecting years of thoughtful stewardship and evident pride of ownership."
      },
